laim","revision":1},{"id":"xpath-array-position","kind":"claim","revision":2},{"id":"xpath-map-constructor","kind":"claim","revision":2},{"id":"xpath31-duplicate-map-key-error","kind":"claim","revision":1},{"id":"xpath31-language-identity","kind":"claim","revision":1},{"id":"york-ycs257-isetl-language-identity","kind":"claim","revision":1},{"id":"york-ycs257-isetl-linda-dialect-identity","kind":"claim","revision":1},{"id":"york-ycs257-isetl-linda-dialect-of-isetl","kind":"claim","revision":1},{"id":"york-ycs257-isetl-linda-distributed-bags","kind":"claim","revision":1}],"dataset":"language-index","dataset_version":"0.1.0-rc.12-main.2","evaluated_at":"2026-11-24T04:04:44Z","exclusions":["Python nonlocal revision 2, import finder revision 1, and ECMAScript OrdinaryGet revision 1 are excluded because of scope or interpretation challenges.","Other candidate identities, aliases, editions, implementations, lineage, and features remain outside the selected population.","Compiler conformance, runtime performance and scheduling, complete history, and cross-version compatibility beyond explicitly cited language changes.","Claim revisions on explicit or evidence-based hold are outside this release selection."],"limitations":["The selected editions, constructs, and history statements cover a subset of the candidate population and available research dimensions.","The source-to-output mapping is the frozen SCES payload and exact linked registry entities. The candidate excludes upstream source text and code.","Proposed Apache-2.0 distribution terms apply to the original Software Commons records and annotations, subject to separate authorization.","C edition identity uses IEC catalog evidence. Technical C findings are limited to WG14 N3220.","The Python implicit-class observation applies to the recorded Windows AMD64 CPython 3.13.0 context. The Visual Basic claims are restricted to the cited Microsoft editions and archive examples.","The governing-source investigation of 47 scoped predecessor planning rows is still open. The census is not a closed language universe.","The vendor SQL dialect records leave the original regex facility lead mappings open. RPG IV and TSO/E REXX retain original-locator access gaps.","The SETL archive records distinguish languages, dialects and implementations. The ISETL link applies to the language referent. The Enterprise COBOL claim applies to the exact documented implementation and leaves conforming behavior outside scope.","The Java technical claims apply to specification edition 21. The census and research profiles remain incomplete.","Prolog chronology and the exact NIP relationship remain unresolved. The historical Prolog records apply to their documented original design.","The resolved SAP links apply to the inspected title, edition and language. The broad ABAP CDS labels retain an open distinction between DDL and DCL.","The classifier links apply only to their assessed programming-language referents. Other file usage, editions, compatibility, and broad alias scopes remain distinct.","Four original ALGOL archive anchors retain overlapping language or implementation scopes.","The broad Oberon classifier remains open. The distinct new Oberon-2 lead is provisional.","The mixed Oberon classifier remains unresolved. The Oberon-2 claims apply to the reported design.","The three exact base-format exclusions are discovery findings. The related selector, schema, encoding, and host-language behaviors require separate evidence.","The SETL variadic read-write parameter case remains unresolved. The PARLOG meta-call claim applies only to the documented proposal.","The three STRling crosswalks identify existing host SQL dialects. Exact installed engines, package configuration, and observed runtime behavior are outside those decisions.","The hardware description cohort uses historical normative texts and selected modern publisher catalog descriptions. It establishes no cross-edition or synthesis conformance.","The mixed historical Lean classifier and Alloy executable repository remain open. TLA and TLA+ retain distinct source scopes.","The Delphi visibility claims apply to the exact Borland 7 guide. The earlier citation remains inconclusive.","The Ruby and C++ technical claims apply to Ruby 3.4.10 documentation and WG21 N4950 respectively. The original STRling regex facilities retain their separate scope.","The HSP claims apply to exact HSP3.7 documentation and a release-pinned OpenHSP README.","Dolittle claims apply to the exact 2001 coauthor publication and its historical interpreter.","SAP ABAP CDS DCL claims apply to Release 754. Both broad ABAP CDS leads remain unresolved across DDL and DCL.","ClojureScript is an independently scoped dialect. The base EDN format exclusion and the unresolved mixed Clojure classifier remain discovery decisions.","Nadesiko identity and edition are bound to project documentation. The implementation observations apply to the exact Nadesiko TypeScript 3.8.12 routines. The v1 edition binding and compatibility remain open.","Python async and cleanup claims apply to the exact 3.13.0 reference. The original async-for limitation remains withheld. The revised claim is restricted to the awaited iteration step and preserves the illustrative outline discrepancy.","SETL2 assertions, procedures and packages apply to the exact 1990 technical report. The all-skip assertion mode selection and default remain unresolved.","Ten STRling links now identify scoped existing host-language referents. The C link rests on exact release and WG14 sources. Separate SCES maintenance reviews resolved the IEC response mismatch for the two exact catalog claims.","There are 1,035 unresolved leads. This candidate covers the measured selected profiles and exact observed scope.","CPL and BCPL design findings retain their exact reports. CPL1, the 1967 and 2026 BCPL documents, and the PDP-11 and Honeywell B implementations retain separate scopes.","Early JOVIAL claims apply to the exact February 1960 and June 1961 SDC documents. The archive report number discrepancy is preserved. J3, J73 and interpreter details remain outside the selected language profile.","REXX research distinguishes Hawes’s ARexx implementation from the language and the exact TSO/E REXX environment. The mixed classifier and query-bearing IBM original retain limited lead decisions.","Smalltalk-80 is a separate documented edition. Blue Book language statements retain their exact book scope. The broader classifier groups different Smalltalk environments and remains unresolved."],"previous_report":{"path":"sces/releases/verified-language-cohort-main-bootstrap-rc1/qualification.json","sha256":"0396e0b66ed1b3182e3fd70eef13fdef3dda2e4e93f4306156157a9ded6ead06"},"release":"verified-language-cohort-main-rc12","research_cutoff":"2026-11-23T11:55:17Z","schema_version":"registry-v1","scope":"Publisher-scoped language identities and selected technical or historical facets for ABAP, ABAP CDS DDL, Ada, Argus, CLU, COBOL, Clojure, Delphi Object Pascal, ECMAScript, Gallina, Go, Haskell, Icon, Informix 4GL, Kotlin, Lua, MUMPS, Modula-3, NESL, Napier88, Oberon, Pascal, PeopleCode, PostgreSQL SQL dialect, Python, REXX, RPG IV, Rust, SIMULA 67, SQL, SQLite SQL dialect, Scala, Visual Basic for .NET, Wolfram Language, XML, XPath. The candidate also covers source-scoped C, classic Visual Basic and its 6.0 edition, VBA, VBScript, and additional Python 3.13.0 and ECMAScript 2024 technical depth. The successor adds Java SE 21, SETL family and vendor SQL dialect records, the exact Gallina origin bridge, and the documented Enterprise COBOL for z/OS 6.4 implementation relationship. The successor includes scoped Prolog and PARLOG archive research, SQR for PeopleSoft, ABAP CDS DCL and additional SAP ABAP evidence. The successor adds scoped Java SE 21 execution and concurrency findings and nine independently agreed language-referent links. The successor adds scoped ALGOL 68 and ALGOL-N archival records and resolves the Ada original at language level. The successor includes the Oberon-2 report dialect, scoped GraphQL, Protocol Buffers schema and TOML profiles, and technical research in ISETL, SETL and PARLOG. The successor includes independently inspected formal and hardware description profiles, Ruby, C++, HSP3.7, and revised Delphi 7 visibility and TLA+ module extension statements. This cohort adds historical Dolittle, Nadesiko and its third edition, ClojureScript, and scoped ABAP CDS DCL Release 754, Python 3.13.0 and SETL2 Technical Report 490 profiles. It adjudicates only the documented Clojure ecosystem, regional and predecessor leads. This cohort adds exact CPL, BCPL, B, early JOVIAL and Smalltalk language records and scoped REXX and ARexx evidence. The Smalltalk-80 edition and ARexx implementation have separate reference identities. Five discovery leads are newly resolved.","source_commit":"10f0544310037d487ba728496fe3f36fc7b6a674"}
